{
  "slug": "artist:de-la-soul",
  "name": "De La Soul",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in 1988 in the Amityville area of Long Island, New York, the hip-hop trio De La Soul gained early acclaim for their eccentric lyrics and eclectic sampling. Comprising Kelvin 'Posdnuos' Mercer, David 'Trugoy the Dove' Jolicoeur, and Vincent 'Maseo' Mason, the group captured the attention of producer Prince Paul with a demo tape of their track 'Plug Tunin''. Their debut studio album, 1989's 3 Feet High and Rising, remains a defining piece of alternative hip-hop, featuring the hit 'Me Myself and I'. A vital component of the Native Tongues Posse, the trio helped push jazz rap forward while maintaining a distinct, constantly shifting style. Over their lengthy career, they have released 10 studio albums, including the cult classic De La Soul Is Dead, which famously signaled the end of their 'D.A.I.S.Y. Age' imagery. In 2006, they earned their first Grammy Award for their collaboration with Gorillaz on the track 'Feel Good Inc.'. Despite long-standing legal disputes with Tommy Boy Records that kept their catalog off streaming services for years, the group regained ownership of their masters and achieved a major digital re-release in 2023. Their 2025 release, Cabin in the Sky, features collaborations with artists including Common, Black Thought, and Nas.",
